Xfile

A library that will ease the often cumbersome usage of the filesystem by
layering auto-backups, entire-file-reading, entire-file-writing, and
possibly file locking (that last one is not that easy - unixes don't do
proper file locking!)

1. lockfile creation - return whether attempt to create lockfile was
   successful (creation of lockfile must be atomic). Lockfile removal
   only allowed when same process + xfile descriptor is used to remove
   the lock.

2. file auto-backup on open for writing - when opened for writing, if
   file exists it must be renamed to file.xback.1. If file.xback.1
   exists, it must be renamed to file.xback.2, etc...

3. Auto-backup extension - must be settable (set to NULL, disables
   backup).

4. size, owner, readable, writable functions needed for files (using 
   pathnames)

5. file listing, directory listing, file removal, directory removal and
   file renaming, directory renaming functions needed for pathnames

6. Swap file backing support.

7. Advise callers to set TMPDIR and/or TMP, or set it for them

8. For reading/writing/seeking/get_position use FILE *: _open_osfhandle
   then _fdopen (win32) to get a FILE *.
